From ec7ba5cd701ad075cd347cab99f34e721a1a0c47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeamHarrisCali <34009957+TeamHarrisCali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:30:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Screen off after (Settings, 2 min default), clean shutdown on
 a critical battery

w99f on the console: "screen off" / "screen on" switch both backlights,
the 2 minute timer and the lid work (lid=closed, screen=off). So:
- screensleep.c: 120 s by default again.
- Settings: a "Screen off" row (never, 30 s, 1, 2, 5, 10, 30 min),
  saved as screenoff= in /home/settings.conf and applied at every
  desktop start (the saved choice, or 2 min); battery and volume share
  one info line so the window still fits.
- dsautolog: at battery level 1 or 0 (the power micro's critical and
  empty), not charging, on two checks 10 s apart, run /boot/shutdown
  (log, sync, power off) instead of losing power during a card write;
  save() uses the same run() helper.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
